From: Swiftly <accounts@paulherter.de>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:55:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: pad direct-rendered MPEG pictures for SIMD motion compensation

FFmpeg software decoders can render directly into libVLC-owned picture
planes. The pinned FFmpeg's avcodec_align_dimensions2() does not reserve the
horizontal edge bytes that MPEG motion-compensation kernels may read. A
frame-edge half-pel vector can therefore read one byte beyond a tightly sized
plane and fault when that plane ends at a VM-region boundary.

VideoLAN MR !8159 applies 32 pixels of horizontal padding for MPEG-1/2 while
waiting for FFmpeg's allocator contract to be corrected. SwiftVLC PR #170
reports the same mpeg_motion -> ff_put_pixels8_x2_neon signature for MPEG-4
Part 2, with the faulting address exactly one byte after a width*height luma
allocation. Apply the narrow allocation workaround to all three codecs. This
keeps direct rendering enabled and avoids the extra full-frame copy imposed
by disabling avcodec-dr globally; hardware-decoded paths are unchanged.

Origin: SwiftVLC (harflabs), scripts/patches/0021-avcodec-mpeg-motion-padding.patch
SwiftVLC is MIT-licensed; this patch modifies VLC and is under VLC's
LGPL-2.1-or-later. Taken over unchanged into Swiftly's VLCKit build.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/video.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
index 8dea45815a..b05449513c 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/video.c
@@ -296,6 +296,7 @@ static int lavc_GetVideoFormat(decoder_t *dec, video_format_t *restrict fmt,
 {
     int width = ctx->coded_width;
     int height = ctx->coded_height;
+    bool needs_motion_padding = false;
 
     video_format_Init(fmt, 0);
 
@@ -314,6 +315,9 @@ static int lavc_GetVideoFormat(decoder_t *dec, video_format_t *restrict fmt,
             fmt->i_chroma = VLC_CODEC_XRGB;
 
         avcodec_align_dimensions2(ctx, &width, &height, aligns);
+        needs_motion_padding = ctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG1VIDEO ||
+                               ctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG2VIDEO ||
+                               ctx->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG4;
     }
 
     if( width == 0 || height == 0 || width > 8192 || height > 8192 ||
@@ -325,6 +329,13 @@ static int lavc_GetVideoFormat(decoder_t *dec, video_format_t *restrict fmt,
         return -1; /* invalid display size */
     }
 
+    /* FFmpeg's SIMD MPEG motion compensation may read beyond the visible
+     * edge. Direct rendering therefore needs horizontal padding in the
+     * libVLC-owned picture, matching FFmpeg-owned frame allocation. Add it
+     * after validating the coded dimensions so 8192-pixel video stays valid. */
+    if (needs_motion_padding)
+        width += 32;
+
     fmt->i_width = width;
     fmt->i_height = height;
     if ( dec->fmt_in->video.i_visible_width != 0 &&
